## THE FIXED TEXT PARTS (approved byte for byte by Tuesday's read-whole; ASCII; one line each; paths and lines at main {SHA})
- `<MOVE-T910>` = This ticket moves to Testing next, under the project's work-tracking rule for a code change (merged, and main's push Build for the merge commit reads success); nothing is deployed.
- `<MOVE-N>` = This ticket does not move in this record; its status is unchanged.
- `<T1-WORDS-FILED>` = filed as the ticket {T1}
- `<T1-WORDS-NOT>` = recorded in the project history and not yet ticketed
- `<T2-WORDS-FILED>` = filed as the ticket {T2}
- `<T2-WORDS-NOT>` = recorded in the project history and not yet ticketed
- `<T1-SUMMARY>` = RD-910 follow-up: a roster read that is a list holding an empty entry still reaches the chat route's later fresh reads (backend/server.js:7314 and :7334), so a user on the roster gets an error text instead of the answer (low)
